00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:16,760
Why not?

278
00:15:17,440 --> 00:15:20,000
Her mom's been cleverly avoiding the investigators.

279
00:15:21,040 --> 00:15:24,460
Child Protective Services went to their house three times to speak with her.

280
00:15:25,240 --> 00:15:28,240
She must have known they were coming because her and Kaio were never home.

281
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,640
So, no official interview has happened yet.

282
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,880
What a bunch of useless people.

283
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:34,840
Well, I said that out loud.

284
00:15:34,840 --> 00:15:38,180
Yes, well, I've spoken with Kaio's mom a number of times.

285
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:41,340
There's no doubt she's abusing her daughter.

286
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:44,440
But I have to wait for CPS to confirm it.

287
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:47,160
When they do, they'll take Kaio away from her.

288
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,620
He's already got this figured out.

289
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:56,060
The thing is, once they intervene and get her to safety, it means she won't be coming back here, ever.

290
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:58,000
I don't care about that.

291
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:00,760
As long as Kaio's safe, the sooner the better.

292
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:06,060
It's almost March, so there's only a few days left to save her.

293
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:09,020
Someone has to do something now.

294
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:11,740
I have to do something.

295
00:16:13,400 --> 00:16:14,520
Sit down, will ya?

296
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,320
Holy shit.

297
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:19,080
Where the hell's everyone's lunch money?

298
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:24,560
You'd think a 29-year-old would be smart enough not to leave cash in his desk.

299
00:16:24,560 --> 00:16:27,480
Mr. Yashiro?

300
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:28,500
What's up?

301
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,460
It's about the lunch money.

302
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:31,940
I can't find it.

303
00:16:34,980 --> 00:16:37,140
Sir, I think I know what happened.

304
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,700
Someone must have stolen it.

305
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,580
And I have a feeling that someone is Kaio.

306
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,320
What?

307
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:43,560
How do you know she did?

308
00:16:43,860 --> 00:16:45,140
Who else could it be?

309
00:16:45,460 --> 00:16:48,080
I mean, she doesn't have to pay for her lunches like we do.

310
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:50,920
His Lord of figures the thief would be someone who's poor.

311
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:52,360
Good boy.

312
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:53,800
Did you take it, Kaio?

313
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:55,800
The brat.

314
00:16:56,880 --> 00:17:00,380
The best way to find out who stole it is to check everyone's bags.

315
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:01,980
She's right, Teach.

316
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,320
We should check them.

317
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:04,260
I just want to eat my lunch.

318
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:05,800
This sucks.

319
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,280
You gonna check your bag?

320
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:08,320
No, what's the point?

321
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:10,080
I already know I didn't take the cash.

322
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,540
Check the bag of the person next to you, too.

323
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:14,340
You stole it, didn't you?

324
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:15,140
Drop, Dad.

325
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:16,820
Hurry, find the thief!

326
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:18,200
I didn't find anything!

327
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,420
I bet it's Kaio.

328
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:20,520
I know, right?

329
00:17:20,660 --> 00:17:21,940
Poor kid, s'more kid!

330
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:24,240
Found it.

331
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:25,700
Where's Kaio?

332
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:26,580
Poor girl did it!

333
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,980
I told you she took it!

334
00:17:28,100 --> 00:17:29,680
Kaio's a thief and should be expelled!

335
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,540
Shut up!

336
00:17:30,820 --> 00:17:32,820
It doesn't matter if she's poor or more hungry!

337
00:17:33,080 --> 00:17:35,260
Kaio would never steal anything from anyone!

338
00:17:35,260 --> 00:17:41,740
I bet you took the money.

339
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:48,000
You know, anyone could have taken the cash from Satoru's desk and planted it in Kaio's bag.

340
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:53,100
Alright, guys.

341
00:17:53,260 --> 00:17:56,960
Remember, Kaio was helping collect the money earlier, so of course she'd have it.

342
00:17:57,340 --> 00:17:59,200
Misato, Satoru, it's over.

343
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:00,600
Okay, everyone.

344
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:01,280
Back to lunch.

345
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:02,300
I knew she didn't.

346
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:02,560
Okay!

347
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:08,520
This isn't awkward.

348
00:18:11,320 --> 00:18:13,260
Thanks for speaking up for me before.

349
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:14,580
Oh, sure.

350
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:16,980
She had no right accusing you.

351
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:19,680
Back in third grade,

352
00:18:20,540 --> 00:18:22,060
Misato made fun of my pencils,

353
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:25,820
so I took her favorite mechanical pencil and chucked it out the window.

354
00:18:25,820 --> 00:18:32,960
Since then, she's hated me like you wouldn't believe, and I hated her right back.

355
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:37,220
This other time, she invited me to a Christmas party at her house.

356
00:18:37,220 --> 00:18:40,420
But that was only to show off how big her tree was.

357
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:43,660
It was really pretty, though.

358
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:47,460
I remember tonight.

359
00:18:49,620 --> 00:18:52,880
Hey, after we're done here, wanna go see one?

360
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:53,840
One what?

361
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,720
A Christmas tree.

362
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,360
You're an idiot.

363
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:58,540
You're an idiot.

364
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:04,280
Here.

365
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,640
You're gonna need him.

366
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:10,360
It gets super cold up on the mountain.

367
00:19:12,060 --> 00:19:14,200
They didn't say I was gonna go with you.

368
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:24,320
I always used to come here to go skiing and bobsledding.

369
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,680
I'd even see a red fox or two.

370
00:19:29,680 --> 00:19:38,440
There they are!

371
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:42,300
Aren't they cool?

372
00:19:42,740 --> 00:19:45,860
I remembered the foxes running around and around.

373
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:49,960
But 18 years ago, I was by myself,

374
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:52,060
and no one believed me when I told them.

375
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:03,200
Were they a couple?

376
00:20:03,720 --> 00:20:04,140
Mm-hmm.

377
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:05,400
I bet they were.

378
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:15,960
The sky's clearing up.

379
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,060
It's a perfect night.

380
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:23,120
There it is.

381
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:41,980
That's a Christmas tree.

382
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:43,320
Huh.

383
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:45,900
Don't be dumb.

384
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:46,900
It's February.

385
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:52,060
We should come back in summer and see it.

386
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:54,140
Our Christmas tree.

387
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,460
You're an idiot.

388
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:27,440
I couldn't answer

389
00:21:27,440 --> 00:21:31,260
The whole thing that I've ever died

390
00:21:31,260 --> 00:21:34,960
Critical improving all of my life

391
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:37,900
My love and happy

392
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:47,680
Next time become as aolina

393
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:50,700
More such things than優しく

394
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:54,640
I opinion it is

395
00:21:54,640 --> 00:22:02,640
子供の頃の僕のままに君のこと

396
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:10,640
守りたいと思う暗闇から目覚めても僕を待ち受けてる

397
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:22,720
彼方で二人を覆したこの街に誰も知らない雪が降っていた

398
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:31,720
君は僕の胸に刻まれた一番深い傷跡のようで

399
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:45,720
君が笑うこの世界の歌乗り戻すよ

